1. Scope

This license covers the project-authored source code, associated documentation,
and executables made from that code that are provided under this license
(the "Software"), only to the extent the relevant copyright holders are
entitled to grant these rights. "Official project" means LanGame Server
Manager maintained by LanGame Team, not a downstream fork.

Separately licensed material is excluded. In particular, third-party code,
fonts, models, game software, data, and media retain their own terms. The
project-owned assets specifically listed in NOTICE are separately covered by
its brand-use permission or MIT grant, as identified there. This license does
not change ownership of your server configuration, saves, logs, or other user
data.

This is a source-available license with use and redistribution restrictions.
It is not an Open Source Initiative open-source license. No rights are granted
except as expressly stated here or in a separate applicable permission.

2. Permitted noncommercial use

Subject to this license, you may, without paying a license fee, view, download,
copy, build, run, study, and privately modify the Software for your own
noncommercial purposes. Private modifications need not be published or
submitted. You may contribute improvements to the official project under
section 5.

You may let players connect to game servers that you operate for these
noncommercial purposes. Player access to a managed game server alone is not
distribution of the Software. Paying your own hosting, electricity, internet,
or model-provider costs does not by itself make your use commercial.

You may share an official, already publicly released distribution unchanged,
in full, and free of charge, preserving its license, NOTICE, and copyright
notices. This does not permit repackaging, substituting your own builds,
releasing unpublished material, or commercial use.

3. Commercial use requires separate permission

Commercial use is not granted. You must obtain separate written authorization
from the relevant rightsholders before any commercial use, including:

- use in a business's operations, internally or on behalf of customers;
- operating game servers that charge entry, subscriptions, memberships, or
  payments for server-related items, privileges, or other benefits;
- selling or renting the Software, commercial hosting or management panels,
  or using the Software to provide paid deployment, maintenance, or services;
- operating servers to earn advertising, commercial sponsorship, or other
  business revenue.

These restrictions apply to both unmodified and modified Software. Charging
only to recover operating costs, or failing to make a profit, does not exempt
a paid server or business activity. Free personal or community use with no
commercial purpose remains permitted under section 2.

An authorization request, donation, or contribution does not itself grant
commercial rights. Requests may be made to the official project's maintainers
through the repository's private contact request process. A maintainer may
grant only rights they own or have been authorized to grant.

4. No independent modified releases

Except for section 5 and rights preserved by section 6, you may not distribute,
publish, sublicense, or make modified versions available to others as an
independent release, product, download, or hosted management service. This
includes modified source code, binaries, installers, containers, and packages,
as well as other software incorporating protected portions of this Software.

The restriction applies whether a release is free or paid, whether its source
is public or private, and whether it uses the LanGame name or a different name.
Publishing source code does not make an independent modified release permitted.

5. Contributions

You may share patches with the official project's maintainers. You may also
create and maintain source forks, branches, and pull requests solely to
propose, discuss, review, and submit improvements to the official project.
Keep the license and notices, identify the contribution purpose and changes,
and do not use this permission to publish independent releases or build
artifacts for general distribution. Submission does not promise acceptance.

Intentionally offering a contribution for review permits the official
maintainers to receive, copy, and review it for that purpose. It does not by
itself accept an additional commercial grant or transfer your copyright.

For inclusion of new contributions, read the repository-root
CONTRIBUTOR_AGREEMENT.md (LanGame Contributor Agreement 1.0) and expressly
confirm the agreement and covered contribution as described in CONTRIBUTING.md.
When accepted, that separate agreement permits the Official Maintainers to
use, modify, and distribute the contribution within LanGame Server Manager,
including official commercial versions and written commercial-use permission
for customers. It does not authorize unrelated products, separate sale of a
contribution, arbitrary relicensing, customer sublicensing, or independent
modified releases by customers. The public receives no additional commercial
or brand rights merely because a contribution was accepted.

A PR, discussion, private modification, or silence does not itself accept
that agreement. Prior contributions retain their existing permissions; any
additional grant for them requires the relevant rightsholder's explicit
confirmation of the covered contribution. Contributors retain copyright and
may independently use their own original material, without acquiring rights
to redistribute the rest of the project.

